The hold on main for X expires while upstream still serves X: the hold no
longer matches and Provenance passes (the expired entry in the unchanged
acks.json is a note; the summary's "hold expired" line makes the routine
escalate). The day before, it still fails.
-- ops --
jappend rules/brave/clean-urls.json [0, "params"] "held_change"
relock
-- head/rules/acks.json --
{"schema": 1, "acks": [], "holds": [
  {"file": "brave-lists/clean-urls.json", "sha256": "${sha:rules/brave/clean-urls.json}",
   "expires": "2026-10-15", "reason": "waiting on brave/adblock-lists#1", "by": "fixture"}
]}
-- base/rules/acks.json --
{"schema": 1, "acks": [], "holds": [
  {"file": "brave-lists/clean-urls.json", "sha256": "${sha:rules/brave/clean-urls.json}",
   "expires": "2026-10-15", "reason": "waiting on brave/adblock-lists#1", "by": "fixture"}
]}
-- ops --
now 2026-10-15
run Provenance
fail held: brave-lists/clean-urls.json
now 2026-10-16
run Provenance
pass
log holds[0] (brave-lists/clean-urls.json) expired on 2026-10-15
